MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8de559a088a5d4d48bb00ae8ccc21165, type: 3}
  m_Name: Asteroid Strike
  crisisName: Asteroid Strike
  ominousWarningText: "A new object has appeared in the heavens. At first it is faint enough that only careful observation reveals it, another point of light among thousands tracked by astronomers each night. Yet its speed and trajectory refuse to fit the patterns expected of ordinary celestial bodies, and new observations only make the calculations more troubling. Independent observatories repeat the measurements and quietly begin exchanging data, each hoping the others will discover an error. The projected path shifts slightly with every refinement, but always in the same direction—closer to our world."
  obviousWarningText: "The calculations are complete. Observatories across the world now reach the same conclusion using independent instruments and models: the object is on a collision course. The remaining uncertainty concerns where it will strike, how much energy it will release, and whether there is enough time to alter its path. Governments quietly move emergency planners into secure facilities while scientists debate interception methods that until now existed mostly in theory. The object has grown bright enough to be identified by experienced observers without specialized equipment, transforming an abstract prediction into something visible in the night sky."
  ominousWarningTurns: 1
  obviousWarningTurns: 1
  durationTurns: 20
  useAgeWindow: 1
  minimumAge: 15
  maximumAge: 19
  mechanic: 14
  minimumRiskScore: 0
